From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:21:12 -0500
Subject: feat: a jar is wiped only when no Space names it

Spaces can share a session, and everything that assumed a jar had one Space
would have lost someone's sign-ins. RemoveSpace wiped the jar of the Space
deleted. It now wipes only when no Space names that jar, a Space with its
session off among them, and leaves nothing on the pending list and asks for no
collection otherwise (sessions S41, S42).

A wipe is checked when it runs as well as when it is asked for. A window's
session can bring back a Space that names a jar a wipe is waiting on, and a
session row can name one a quit left pending; neither is wiped (S44).

Clear Independent Session tells every Space with that session on, so each
window reloads their tabs (S46). A jar several Spaces name belongs to the Space
on screen when it uses the jar, else the first that uses it: a Space with its
session off had stood in front of one with it on (S49).

An essential of a session shows in every Space of that session, and stays with
the session when the Space it is filed under leaves or is deleted (S47).

Changing a Space's session goes through the registry, so every window moves the
Space's tabs by the road a session turned on takes, a page with unsaved changes
kept where it is (S40). Moving away erases nothing, and a session no Space uses
ends only by DeleteUnusedSession (S43, S45).

Why: the wipe was the one place this feature could lose a user's data (ADR
0032).

Removable when: never; it is what makes a shared session safe.
